## Repair summary — D9-cheeger-gromov-compactness

**Root cause (attempt 1 compile-gate failure).** `gate.json` had been removed by the dispatcher when it queued the repair, so I reproduced the gate exactly (`longrun/bin/dispatch_loop.py::compile_gate` semantics). The failure was **not** in any `.lean` source: the build artifacts of the four D9 modules were absent from `release/.lake/build/lib/lean/Poincare/D9/CheegerGromov/`, so the two files importing sibling modules died at import resolution:

```
AxiomAudit.lean:1:0: error: object file '.../.lake/build/lib/lean/Poincare/D9/CheegerGromov/PointedConvergence.olean'
of module Poincare.D9.CheegerGromov.PointedConvergence does not exist
```

The worktree's `release/.lake` had been restored to the pristine D6 build tree (no `Poincare/D9` directory; surviving olean mtimes Sep 9 11:49), while the `.lean` sources were untouched.

**Fix (authored files unchanged).**
- `cd release && lake build Poincare.D9.CheegerGromov.AxiomAudit` → exit 0, 8884 jobs; all four D9 modules built (`logs/repair_d9_build.log`). This repopulates exactly the oleans the root gate resolves through `.lake → release/.lake`.
- Full dispatcher-gate replica re-run: **68/68 files exit 0**, 0 failures, 237.5 s (`logs/repair_gate_result.json`, `logs/repair_gate_run2.log`).
- Four D9 files re-elaborated from the worktree root: all exit 0; `AxiomAudit` still prints 77/77 standard cones (`logs/repair_rootgate_*.log`).
